# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows and runs on Linux. A CRLF checkout puts a
# carriage return on the shebang line, and the container then fails to start
# with "/usr/bin/env: bash\r: No such file or directory" -- which takes the
# whole Hub down, not just the tool whose script it is, and reads like a
# missing interpreter rather than a line-ending problem.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
